    "name": "PU Embossed Stickers",
    "shortDescriptionHtml": "<h2>Material Depth. Sophisticated Texture. Engineered Branding.</h2><p>Elevate your brand with the “Material Depth” of our PU Embossed Stickers. Designed for those who prioritize a refined, leather-like aesthetic, these labels combine a soft-touch matte finish with a structured multi-layer build. Unlike traditional flat prints, our PU labels feature a cushioned, convex elevation that highlights your logo with subtle, non-reflective dimension.</p><ul><li><p><b>Tactile Finish:</b> Premium matte grain with a soft-touch, leather-like feel.</p></li><li><p><b>Engineered Build:</b> Multi-layer construction for durable, structured depth.</p></li><li><p><b>Precision Elevation:</b> Soft-contoured “convex” effects for a natural, integrated look.</p></li><li><p><b>High-End Durability:</b> Water-resistant, scratch-proof, and built for permanent adhesion.</p></li></ul><p>Ideal for fashion apparel, tech accessories, and luxury product packaging.</p>",
    "descriptionHtml": "<h2>Premium Multi-Layer Stickers with Texture, Structure, and Adhesion</h2><p>PU Stickers are built for branding that relies on material presence, not surface print. With a leather-like matte finish and a defined multi-layer construction, they introduce depth, softness, and structure in a single application.</p><p>They don’t just sit on a surface – they become part of it.</p><h2>Surface That Doesn’t Feel Flat</h2><p>PU embossed stickers are designed to create a quiet premium effect:</p><ul><li><strong>Soft-touch surface</strong> with a leather-like feel</li><li><strong>Matte, non-reflective finish</strong> for a clean visual tone</li><li><strong>Fine grain texture</strong> that mimics natural leather</li><li>A controlled, structured feel – not too rigid, not too flexible</li></ul><p>The fine grain texture is a subtle micro-texture across the surface that breaks flatness, diffuses light, and gives the label a more natural, material-like appearance rather than a printed look.</p><h2>Multi-Layer Construction (Engineered Feel)</h2><p>What sets PU embossed label apart is how they are built – not just how they look.</p><p>Each label consists of a layered structure that creates both texture and durability:</p><ul><li><strong>Top Layer (PU Surface)</strong><br>\nA matte, leather-like surface with fine grain texture. This layer defines the tactile experience – soft, slightly textured, and visually refined.</li><li><strong>Core / Body Layer</strong><br>\nProvides thickness, structure, and dimensional stability. This layer allows controlled build-up within the label, contributing to its dimensional presence.</li><li><strong>Adhesive Layer</strong><br>\nA pressure-sensitive backing that ensures clean, consistent application across surfaces.</li></ul><p>Together, these layers create a label that is:</p><ul><li>Soft to touch yet structurally stable</li><li>Flexible enough to conform, but not flimsy</li><li>Visually clean, yet physically dimensional</li></ul><h2>Convex Raised Effect (Material-Based Elevation)</h2><p>Embossed stickers allow specific areas of the design to be selectively raised above the base surface, creating a soft convex, protruding effect.</p><p>This is achieved by building up selected areas within the internal structure layer, rather than pressing or stamping the material.</p><ul><li>The chosen design elements protrude outward from the label surface</li><li>The PU top layer wraps smoothly over these raised areas</li><li>The result is a rounded, soft elevation – not sharp or rigid</li><li>Transitions between raised and flat areas remain clean and seamless</li></ul><p>The effect feels:</p><ul><li>Cushioned when touched</li><li>Noticeably lifted above the surrounding surface</li><li>Visually dimensional under light</li><li>Fully integrated into the material, not applied on top</li></ul><p>This creates a refined protruding depth that highlights key elements without relying on gloss or heavy effects.</p><h2>Built for Real-World Use</h2><ul><li><strong>Water-resistant</strong> → suitable for everyday handling</li><li><strong>Scratch-resistant</strong> → maintains a clean surface over time</li><li><strong>Indoor &amp; outdoor compatibility</strong> → adaptable across applications</li></ul><p>They are designed to hold both their form and finish.</p><p><strong>Customization</strong><strong> (Keeps It Simple)</strong></p><ul><li>Die-cut to any shape</li><li>Custom sizes</li><li>Any color matching your brand</li><li>Matte leather-like finish</li></ul><p>Each label is produced to align with your design intent and brand identity.</p><h2>Application Versatility</h2><p>PU embossed stickers are widely used across:</p><ul><li>Fashion and apparel branding</li><li>Premium packaging</li><li>Product labeling</li><li>Medical or functional applications</li></ul><p>They provide a consistent material language across different touchpoints.</p><p>Depending on the desired finish, some brands also explore alternatives such as Custom Puffy Stickers for a more tactile, foam-based effect or 3D Epoxy Stickers for a polished, reflective surface.</p><h2>A Note on Material Evolution</h2><p>While traditional faux leather stickers are typically used as stitched tags, embossed adhesive labels bring a similar leather-like aesthetic into an adhesive format, allowing for faster, cleaner, and more scalable application.</p><h2>Packaging Options</h2><ul><li><strong>Individual pieces</strong> → ready for direct use</li><li><strong>Sheets</strong> → optimized for bulk handling</li></ul><h2>A Different Kind of Branding Surface</h2><p>PU labels don’t rely on gloss, shine, or heavy effects.<br>\nThey rely on layering, texture, and restraint.</p><p>For brands looking for a softer, more playful dimension, options like Custom Puffy Stickers offer a thicker, cushioned feel, while 3D Epoxy Stickers focus on a high-gloss, domed finish.</p><p>That’s what gives them presence.</p><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h2>Check out our Epoxy Stickers FAQ’s below:</h2><p><br><a>How are PU embossed stickers different from faux leather labels?</a></p><p>Faux leather labels are typically non-adhesive and used as sewn tags. PU stickers are adhesive-backed, allowing them to function as stickers while maintaining a leather-like appearance.</p><p><a>Are embossed labels waterproof?</a></p><p>They are water-resistant and suitable for everyday use, including light outdoor exposure.</p><p><a>What surfaces can PU embossed stickers be applied to?</a></p><p>PU stickers can be applied to a variety of surfaces including packaging materials, plastics, paper-based products, and certain fabrics, depending on the application.</p><p><a>Can embossed stickers be customized in shape and size?</a></p><p>Yes, PU stickers can be die-cut into any custom shape and produced in a wide range of sizes based on your design requirements.</p><p><a>Do PU stickers have a matte or glossy finish?</a></p><p>PU embossed stickers feature a matte, leather-like finish with a fine grain texture, giving them a premium and refined appearance.</p><p><a>What is the difference between PU stickers, puffy stickers, and 3D epoxy stickers?</a></p><p>The difference comes down to material, structure, and surface effect:</p><ul><li><strong>PU </strong><strong>Embossed Stickers</strong><br>\nBuilt using a multi-layer construction, PU stickers have a matte, leather-like textured surface with a soft-touch feel. Selected areas can be raised in a convex, protruding form, creating a controlled, material-based depth rather than a glossy or exaggerated 3D effect.</li><li><strong>Puffy Stickers</strong><br>\nMade using foam layers, they create a soft, thick, cushion-like 3D feel with more noticeable height and playful dimension.</li><li><strong>3D Epoxy Stickers</strong><br>\nCoated with a clear resin layer, they have a smooth, glossy dome finish that creates a high-shine, glass-like appearance with strong light reflection.</li></ul><p>Each option offers a different tactile and visual experience, depending on whether the goal is subtle material depth, soft elevation, or high-gloss impact.</p>",
